<urn:atm:triage:finding/WINTEST-001-AL8>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "WINTEST-001-AL8" ;
  triage:title "owner_gate.rs Windows file-lock test failure — DaemonOwnerGuard holds exclusive OS lock while test re-opens same file for reading" ;
  triage:description "Test owner_record_uses_the_local_http_instance_schema at crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/owner_gate.rs panics ONLY on windows-latest CI (GH Actions run https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/actions/runs/31154828298, job 92792110253) with: Os { code: 33, kind: Uncategorized, message: \"The process cannot access the file because another process has locked a portion of the file.\" } at approximately owner_gate.rs:94 (std::fs::read_to_string(&lock) inside the test). Root cause: DaemonOwnerGuard::acquire_at (same file, introduced by commit f28ee24e 'feat(AL.8): activate Tokio Axum daemon composition') opens the owner-record file with an fs2::FileExt exclusive lock and keeps that File handle (and lock) alive for the guard's lifetime. The test holds the guard alive while separately opening the same path a second time via std::fs::read_to_string. Unix advisory flock() does not block that second open/read, but Windows LockFileEx-based locking does, so the test only fails on windows-latest." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "portability-lint" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-07T07:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
